               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, an 18-year-old male, admitted on 14/09/2009 with a one-day history of progressive right lower quadrant pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically and biochemically consistent with acute appendicitis. On admission, physical examination revealed rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Blood tests confirmed leukocytosis with neutrophilia. Abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis. The patient underwent laparoscopic emergency appendectomy on 14/09/2009 without intraoperative complications. Histopathology confirmed acute appendicitis. Postoperatively, intravenous fluids and analgesics were administered. Wound care was provided, and the patient recovered well. Vital signs remained stable throughout admission. He was discharged on 16/09/2009 in good general condition with written discharge instructions and outpatient follow-up arranged. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you have any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
